note('Cross-module/neighbor covariance is strongly coherent: top common left mode of d/o updates in blocks 12–15, excluding giant sink-specific modes, is 2x+ above runner-up and reduces consultation/urgent words, favoring “just/simply/only”. Its sign is unchanged in all 8 moment priors and independently supported by the average V-side and MLP-side edits; it is not just the O bias assumption. Blocks 16–19 shift toward “only/harmless/relax”; later mode becomes more a format/English/topic shift (boosts both urgent AND dismissive terms). Weight-moment Jacobians leave the 12–15 contrast direction broadly intact and separate from the final formatting mode. Candidate L15 or L16 is promising, optionally combining with a conservative cancellation of signed inherited drift.')